DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T140000
UID:6a1f2b568360de907d892dfd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:À partir de chants et histoires de la Louisiane\, Bill Russel
 l avive son jeune public. Tout le monde est invité à participer durant l
 e spectacle. Il raconte avec un sourire dans un coin de la bouche le pass
 é et le présent des Cajuns et leurs liens avec les Acadiens.\nFeaturing 
 songs and stories from Louisiana\, Bill Russell enlivens his young audienc
 e. Everyone is invited to participate during the show. He recounts with a 
 smile in the corner of his mouth the past and present of the Cajuns and th
 eir links with the Acadians.\nRegistration is required. Register here or c
 all 416-396-8939 to register.
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1f2b568360de907d892dfd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
