SUMMARY:Toronto Reference Library Summer Tours!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T160000
UID:6a301f054407827f8aa50904@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wanted to learn more about our collections at th
 e Toronto Reference Library? Are you curious about what specific features 
 and services are available on all of the floors? From piano rooms for reci
 tal practice\, to 3D print stations for toy modelling\, we explore all the
  amazing things that this building has to offer. Join us for a free guide
 d tour of the Toronto Reference Library! Please meet at the Main floor by 
 the stage.\nNo Registration is required.\nNote:\nFor larger group tours\, 
 please email our Toronto Reference Library User Education Department to ar
 range a booking: trlusereducation@tpl.ca
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Meeting place: Main floor\, by the st
 age.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a301f054407827f8aa50904
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toys Alive! Exhibition Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T173000
UID:69fdddb5c6a1dc3d00d258a8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about what your toys get up to when you are not lookin
 g? We jumped into the toy box to discover just that. From dolly’s advent
 ures to teddy bears on the search for honey to toy soldiers on patrol. Joi
 n us for a free guided tour of TD Gallery’s current exhibition Toys Aliv
 e! Explore literary works from the late 1800s to present day from the Osbo
 rne Collection of Early Children’s Books!\nRegistration is not required 
 but is encouraged. Please meet at the entrance to the TD Gallery.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, TD Gallery\, first floor of Toronto R
 eference Library
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fdddb5c6a1dc3d00d258a8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:World Cup Henna
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T120000
UID:6a3004fdc7d3cd5800607789@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Henna art is an ancient form of body art\, used in various cel
 ebrations from different parts of the world. It is prepared with the fines
 t blend of henna powder and essential oils like lavender\, eucalyptus\, an
 d/or cajeput oil. Learn about henna art\, practice using it\, and receive 
 a special World Cup design by a professional henna artist.\nFor children a
 ges 6 and up\, teens and adults. Please register everyone attending.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3004fdc7d3cd5800607789
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hands-On Dinosaur Fossils & Ancient Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260902T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260902T143000
UID:6a1d8c1b2ea730c17ab34bcb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an opportunity to handle\, examine up close and di
 scuss nine real and replica fossils in this fascinating hands-on workshop.
  Participants will be entertained and educated\, not just about the fossil
 s themselves\, but the paleontological aspects that underpin them. Concept
 s include: evolution\, fossilization\, ‘The Tree of Life’ (phylogeny) 
 and — of course — dinosaurs!\nFor children ages 6-12. Parents are wel
 come to stay during the program\, but please only register children.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1d8c1b2ea730c17ab34bcb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
