DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T150000
UID:6a3291942ea730c17ab78a5f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this digital literacy program for kids (8+)\, participants 
 will work in teams to answer Jeopardy-style questions!\nCategories will in
 clude: Digital Literacy 101\, Online Safety (privacy\, cyberbullying\, onl
 ine ethics\, etc)\, Fake News\, Balanced Screen Time (stats\, mental heal
 th\, etc.)\, & Cool Concepts (cool\, futuristic things with digital lit e
 .g.\, AI).\nThere will be five questions ranging from 100 to 500 points fo
 r each category\, as well as tiebreaker questions at the end. Have fun l
 earning about these important topics while playing this Jeopardy-style ga
 me!\nThis is a program for kids ages 8-12 years old!\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
